  "summary": "Lightwell Security Advisory: postgresql 42.3.3.rhlw-00006",
  "details": "Red Hat Lightwell has released org.postgresql:postgresql 42.3.3.rhlw-00006 with backported fixes for CVE-2022-31197, CVE-2022-41946, CVE-2024-1597, and CVE-2026-42198.\n\nCVE-2022-31197: SQL Injection in ResultSet.refreshRow() with malicious column names in pgjdbc\n\nCVE-2022-41946: TemporaryFolder on unix-like systems does not limit access to created files in pgjdbc\n\nCVE-2024-1597: pgjdbc SQL Injection via line comment generation\n\nCVE-2026-42198: pgjdbc: Unbounded PBKDF2 iterations in SCRAM authentication allows CPU exhaustion DoS\n\nThis patched artifact is a drop-in replacement for org.postgresql:postgresql 42.3.3 from Maven Central.",
